    "chunk_size_bytes": 1089,
    "chunk_text": "70% of prison population linked to drug addiction, overcrowding concerns raised\n\nColombo, July 2 (Daily Mirror) - Around 70 per cent of the prison population comprises individuals addicted to narcotic substances, highlighting a major challenge facing the country\u2019s correctional system, the President\u2019s Media Division (PMD) said.\n\nAttention was therefore drawn to the urgent need for measures focused on rehabilitation as well as steps to ease prison overcrowding.\n\nThe PMD said the\u00a0 issue was discussed in the context of ongoing national efforts to address the growing impact of drug abuse, with emphasis placed on strengthening rehabilitation programmes for affected individuals.\n\nAuthorities said that improving treatment and recovery pathways for drug-dependent inmates is essential to reducing pressure on prisons while supporting their reintegration into society.\n\nThe findings have reinforced calls for a more coordinated national approach that combines enforcement with rehabilitation-focused strategies to address the root causes of incarceration linked to narcotic addiction."
