    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe see Australia as a market that is ready to move beyond the hype surrounding AI and focus on practical application and measurable business outcomes. From SMEs and entrepreneurs to agencies and larger enterprises, our role is to help organisations bridge the gap between possibility and execution by translating emerging technologies into practical marketing solutions that drive growth, improve efficiency, and create meaningful customer experiences,\u201d said Lahiru Halkewela, Co-Founder of Enfection.\n\nDrawing on extensive experience across sectors such as pharma, education, finance, and retail, Enfection aims to deliver solutions across four core pillars: intelligence, creativity, automation, and gamified platforms/experiences. Each of these pillars is infused with cutting edge AI technology, helping businesses scale efficiently while achieving stronger, more measurable returns on their marketing investments. Beyond its commercial work, Enfection remains committed to community engagement, particularly among the Sri Lankan diaspora in Australia. Initiatives such as a gamified digital Vesak platform allowed Sri Lankans living in Australia to stay connected to their culture, traditions, and heritage. These initiatives reflect Enfection\u2019s broader philosophy that technology and culture can move forward together.\n\nWith offices now established in Colombo, Kuala Lumpur, and Melbourne, Enfection claims they it is well positioned to make AI powered marketing transformation a key export opportunity for Sri Lanka. The company aims to compete confidently with established regional players, backed by a superior understanding of local markets, deep technical expertise in Applied AI, and a track record of effective delivery."
