    "chunk_size_bytes": 1532,
    "chunk_text": "Furkan advises Boards and CEOs on strategy, market expansion, and geopolitical, economic, and technology risk management, and currently serves as CEO of Tresync, Australia. He holds several Board directorships across the Asia-Pacific region, including Senior Independent Director of Asiri Health PLC and Asiri Surgical Hospital PLC, and Independent Non-Executive Director of Odel PLC, Softlogic Capital PLC, Softlogic Holdings PLC, and Diamond Life Insurance Company in Bangladesh. He previously served as CEO of the Sri Lanka Association for Software and Services Companies (SLASSCOM) and Sri Lanka Press Institute, and is a Fellow Member of both CPA Australia and CIMA UK, holding an MBA from Australia and a BA (Hons) from the UK.\n\nVijayananth is an entrepreneur who has thrived in the logistics and food and beverage industries from a young age, and has been instrumental in developing a solid client base across Maharaja Foods and its subsidiary and associate companies. He led the restructuring of the company from a family-oriented partnership into a Group with dedicated business units in retail, logistics, and food and beverage. In his new role, he will focus on retail expansion and new venture development. He holds a Degree in Business Management, specialising in Economics and Consulting, from Aston University.\n\nVithyanath continues in his role as Managing Director of Maharaja Foods PLC, providing continuity in the leadership of the company\u2019s day-to-day operations as the Board transitions into its new structure."
