    "md5": "886b159bad5f8720ffb70ba6b37edc63",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1871,
    "chunk_text": "Uber expands to Ratnapura\n\nUber has announced the launch of Uber Eats and Uber Rides in Ratnapura, further expanding its footprint across the country.\n\nResidents and visitors can now access food, groceries, everyday essentials, and reliable transportation through the Uber app, while local merchants, delivery partners, and drivers gain new opportunities to grow and earn.\n\nUber Sri Lanka Country Manager \u2013 Delivery Varun Wijewardane said: \u201cRatnapura is home to a vibrant community of local businesses and entrepreneurs, and we\u2019re excited to bring Uber Eats to the district. By connecting local merchants with more customers and creating flexible earning opportunities for delivery partners, we hope to make everyday convenience more accessible while supporting local economic growth.\u201d\n\nUber Sri Lanka Country Manager \u2013 Mobility Kaushalya Gunaratne said: \u201cWe\u2019re excited to bring Uber Rides to Ratnapura and make reliable, affordable mobility available to more people across the district. This launch creates new earning opportunities for local drivers while giving residents and visitors access to convenient transportation backed by technology designed to make every trip safer and more seamless.\u201d\n\nWith doorstep pickups available across multiple vehicle categories, Uber Rides offers flexibility and choice for different travel needs and budgets. Every trip is supported by technology-driven safety features including GPS tracking, trip sharing, driver identity verification, in-app emergency assistance, and 24/7 support.\n\nThe launch in Ratnapura builds on Uber\u2019s continued expansion across Sri Lanka. It also marks Uber Eats\u2019 second city launch of the year, following Nuwara Eliya, and follows the recent expansion of Uber Rides to Kegalle, reflecting Uber\u2019s commitment to bringing its technology platform to more communities across the country."
  },
