    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e7d86c9e971d2d4004911dcc7291d775",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1635,
    "chunk_text": "SLT-MOBITEL unveils \u2018Lankakonect\u2019 app with Foreign Affairs Ministry\n\nSLT\u2011MOBITEL, in collaboration with the Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Ministry, has officially launched the Lankakonect mobile application.\n\nUnveiled recently at Cinnamon Lakeside Colombo, the app represents a significant breakthrough in the nation\u2019s digital transformation journey. Acting as a complaint management platform for Sri Lankans living and working abroad, the Lankakonet app eases their ability to raise and track grievances with the relevant authorities.\n\nDeveloped by SLT-MOBITEL for the Ministry\u2019s Consular Affairs Division and the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE), the app offers Sri Lankan overseas citizens and migrant workers worldwide a secure platform to register, submit, and track complaints covering employment contract violations, abuse, unpaid wages, the whereabouts of loved ones, and other concerns in Sinhala, Tamil, and English.\n\nBy moving the process online, the Lankakonect app removes long waits and unnecessary travel, allowing grievances to be raised anywhere, at any time. Domestic workers, ranking high among the most vulnerable, can escalate urgent concerns immediately. Upon lodging a complaint, officials from the SLBFE and Consular Affairs Division can access the system online and beginning working to resolve issues on behalf of the petitioner. Each complaint can be tracked in real time through its full lifecycle, providing users live updates, with management viewing progress. Furthermore, it allows the Ministry to offer a holistic view of the complaint resolution\u2019s progress."
  },
