    "md5": "7929e4dade5527edba73075761745bf2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1855,
    "chunk_text": "Adhitya Ayurveda takes traditional Sri Lankan Ayurveda expertise to South Korea\n\nAdhitya Ayurveda, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading holistic healing organisations, has taken its latest step in its international journey through a wellness knowledge-sharing program conducted in South Korea in collaboration with Shriveda Ayurveda Korea.\n\nThe informative session was led by Dr. Kasun Gunawardhana, who shared the principles of authentic Sri Lankan Ayurveda and its relevance in addressing the health challenges of modern lifestyles.\n\nThe presentation focused on several key areas including Ayurvedic detoxification, preventive wellness, digestive health, Panchakarma therapies, pulse diagnosis, and practical daily routines that support long-term physical and mental wellbeing.\n\nDrawing upon centuries of traditional wisdom, Dr. Gunawardhana highlighted how Ayurveda views health not merely as the absence of disease, but as a harmonious balance between body, mind, and soul. Participants were introduced to the concept of \u201cAma\u201d (toxin accumulation), the importance of digestive strength, and simple yet effective lifestyle practices that can help restore balance in today\u2019s demanding world.\n\nThe event also showcased the unique value of Sri Lankan Ayurvedic traditions, including the use of medicinal herbs, natural ingredients, and personalized healing approaches that have been preserved and practiced for generations. Through engaging discussions and knowledge exchange, participants gained a deeper understanding of how traditional healing systems can complement modern wellness goals.\n\nThis collaboration between Adhitya Ayurveda and Shriveda Ayurveda Korea represents a shared vision of making authentic Ayurvedic knowledge accessible to a wider international audience while building meaningful bridges between cultures through health and wellness."
  },
