    "chunk_text": "Closing shop \u2013 final duties before retiring after 37 years of service\n\nBefore I left for Paris in late November, I had made arrangements to hold the Sri Lanka Education Administrative Service interviews for promotion to Class I of the Service the moment I returned. These interviews had been held up for a number of years due to controversy and serious differences of opinion as to the determination of the seniority list of the service. The various Associations representing these officers could not agree, and some of them went to Court. Pending action in Court and due to other differences the whole process had come to a complete halt.\n\nIn the meantime, Class I of the service was almost empty of officers whilst some of them were retiring and others dying without any hope of their being considered for promotion. This affected their salaries and would have affected their pensions. This was a situation serious from the official point of view and tragic from the personal point of view. I had previously held a number of meetings with the Associations and at last and with great difficulty succeeded in arriving at a consensus.\n\nIn this, Secretaryfor Shipping and Port Development, Mr. M.N. Junaid, who had great experience in establishment matters in the course of a long stay in the Ministry of Public Administration, greatly assisted me in response to my appeal to him. Because of the backlog and because three times the number as there were vacancies had to be called for interviews, the numbers involved were very large. The Minister, after discussion, went to Cabinet and obtained its authority to constitute two Preliminary Interview Boards chaired by Additional Secretaries to weed out the obviously unsuitable and put up for final interviews before a Board to be chaired by me and two other Secretaries of Cabinet Level Ministers, only those they considered eligible for final interview."
  },
