    "chunk_text": "In this, Secretaryfor Shipping and Port Development, Mr. M.N. Junaid, who had great experience in establishment matters in the course of a long stay in the Ministry of Public Administration, greatly assisted me in response to my appeal to him. Because of the backlog and because three times the number as there were vacancies had to be called for interviews, the numbers involved were very large. The Minister, after discussion, went to Cabinet and obtained its authority to constitute two Preliminary Interview Boards chaired by Additional Secretaries to weed out the obviously unsuitable and put up for final interviews before a Board to be chaired by me and two other Secretaries of Cabinet Level Ministers, only those they considered eligible for final interview.\n\nI was by now about to leave for Paris, and feeling seriously exhausted. Therefore, I thought it would be some relief if I could hop across to London from Paris after the conference and just rest and sleep for a couple of days before I got back home to attend to winding up operations and discharging my final responsibility of finishing the interviews. The press of work was such that peace was not possible to attain when one reached Sri Lanka. There was a meeting with the President about four or five days before my departure and since in any case she would have had to approve the number of days I would be out of the country, I thought of informing her personally about taking a couple of days off in London."
