    "md5": "38670f364e03ed87e8dbf7d82d12a4e8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1667,
    "chunk_text": "About a year after my return from Japan, I accepted a more senior appointment at another state-owned enterprise. Although considerably smaller than the Tyre Corporation, the organisation gave me much greater authority and freedom to introduce new ideas.\n\nI immediately recognised an opportunity to put into practice everything I had learnt in Japan.\n\nRather than transplanting the Japanese model wholesale, I redesigned it to suit Sri Lankan organisational culture.\n\nInstead of focusing exclusively on improvements in quality and productivity, I placed equal emphasis on enriching the quality of employees\u2019 working lives. My belief was that if people genuinely enjoyed participating, felt respected and found meaning in their work, improvements in quality and productivity would naturally follow.\n\nI also modified the structure of the circles to better suit our own organisational environment and deliberately introduced an element of enjoyment into the meetings and presentations.\n\nThe Quality Circles became highly successful. Employees participated enthusiastically, managers began to recognise their value and improvements started appearing throughout the organisation.\n\nFor the first time, I became convinced that Quality Circles could indeed flourish in Sri Lanka\u2014provided they were thoughtfully adapted rather than blindly copied.\n\nThat conviction would shape the next chapter of my professional life.\n\nA new life in Saudi Arabia and Romance en route in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
