    "chunk_text": "Uncle Julian was delighted, and on our return, my father killed two \u2018red legs\u2019 birds for dinner. We walked silently for a short distance on an unpaved, narrow path. Uncle Julian stopped and asked my father, \u201cYou do not go to church on Sundays, do you?\n\nWe continued walking silently. The sun was setting and it was a glorious sunset. Julian muttered to himself, \u201cEvery day, God gives us a clue to indicate we are his children. This beautiful sunset demonstrates it \u2013 only fools, especially those possessed by demons, cannot see it.\u201d He wanted me to hear him, but I was not interested in sermons. I did not want to think about gods or my soul, but wanted to play with my dog, Blacky, and my three brothers.\n\nThat night, I could not sleep as I was tormented by the thought of \u2018soul\u2019. I thought God had punished me by making me sleepless for not believing in him. I was scared this punishment would continue day after day. The following morning, I asked my father, \u201cDo I have a soul?\u201d He hesitated for a few seconds and told me that he did not know.\n\nI asked him, \u201cDo you have a soul?\u201d He said, \u201cNo.\u201d He did not want to carry on the discussion. He said, \u201cDo not worry about your soul. When you grow up, you will understand.\u201d When he heard that I could not sleep, he blamed Uncle Julian for trying to inculcate guilt in my mind.\n\nWhile thinking about my soul, it occurred to me that my sister died several years ago. I wanted to know what had happened to her soul. I knew her dead body was interred at a cemetery. I broached the subject with my father again during a weekend. He was willing to discuss the topic of the soul with me. He told me that, being Catholics, we were supposed to believe that each human being has an eternal soul given by God. He used to think that he had a soul, but after going through many difficulties throughout his life, he abandoned the idea of God and soul. My"
