    "chunk_size_bytes": 1604,
    "chunk_text": "Prof. Fazeeha Azmi becomes Lanka\u2019s first woman envoy to Iran\n\nProfessor Fazeeha Azmi has assumed duties as Sri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador-designate to Iran, becoming the country\u2019s first woman to be appointed to the post.She formally took up her duties at the Sri Lankan Embassy in Tehran on June 30.\n\nAddressing embassy staff, Prof. Azmi outlined the Government\u2019s foreign policy priorities and underscored the importance of strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s longstanding relations with Iran, as well as with Azerbaijan and Turkmenistan, to which she is also concurrently accredited.\n\nShe identified trade, employment, education, pharmaceuticals, tourism and cultural cooperation as key areas for expanding bilateral engagement, while calling for renewed efforts to attract Iranian tourists to Sri Lanka in collaboration with the country\u2019s outbound travel industry.\n\nPrior to her diplomatic appointment, Prof. Azmi served as Professor of Geography at the University of Peradeniya, with over two decades of academic and research experience in migration, tourism, post-war development, urban heritage and poverty studies.\n\nA graduate of the University of Peradeniya, she obtained her M.Phil. and Ph.D. from the Norwegian University of Science and Technology. She has also held academic positions in Sri Lanka, India, Norway, Fiji and Canada.\n\nIChemC Annual Sessions 2026 inaugurated with focus on scientific excellence\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
