    "chunk_text": "CaFFE holds digital voter education programme in Jaffna\n\nThe Campaign for Free and Fair Elections (CaFFE) on Wednesday conducted a digital voter education programme in the Jaffna District using the \u201cLearn, Play, Vote\u201d gaming application developed with the support of LIRNEasia.\n\nThe programme, aimed at educating young voters on the electoral process through an interactive digital platform, was held under the leadership of CaFFE Executive Director Surangi Ariyawansha.\n\nFormer Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation News Director and digital media trainer Junaid M. Harish, Head of the Department of Political Science at the University of Jaffna and President of the University\u2019s Teachers\u2019 Association Dr. Vigneswaran, and former Head of the Department of Economics and Senior Lecturer at the University of Jaffna C. Udayakumar served as resource persons.\n\nSenior Research Manager at LIRNEasia Isuru Samarathunga attended the event as the chief guest.\n\nParticipants were introduced to key aspects of the electoral process through the innovative digital platform, which combines learning with interactive gameplay to promote greater awareness of democratic participation among young people.\n\nAIA\u2019s first \u2018Dansala on a Train\u2019 takes the spirit of local hospitality onboard\n\nIChemC Annual Sessions 2026 inaugurated with focus on scientific excellence\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
