    "chunk_text": "Royal clinch Western Province Hockey title in penalty shootout\n\nRoyal College, Colombo were crowned Western Province Hockey champions after edging defending champions St. Joseph\u2019s College, Colombo in a dramatic penalty shootout following a 1-1 draw in the final at the Colombo International Astro Turf ground.\n\nThe tournament, organised by the Western Province Ministry of Education, was held from June 19 to 23.\n\nRoyal dominated possession for much of the contest with fluent passing and attacking play, taking the lead in the ninth minute when centre forward Kithmina Rathnayake converted a rebound from a penalty corner. St. Joseph\u2019s fought back in the closing stages, with captain Mark Ruiz equalising after capitalising on a defensive lapse. The Josephians missed a late penalty corner opportunity that could have secured victory.\n\nThe initial five-player penalty shootout ended 3-3, forcing sudden death. Royal\u2019s Rumal Jayasinghe converted his effort before goalkeeper Stefan Anthonypillai produced the decisive save against St. Joseph\u2019s vice-captain Raghavan Gokul to seal the title.\n\nThe victory gave Royal their second major title within a month, having also won the All-Island Championship in May. Royal reached the final unbeaten, defeating Bandaranayake College Gampaha (6-0), Isipathana College (3-0) and Prince of Wales\u2019 College, Moratuwa (3-1). Prince of Wales\u2019 secured third place by beating St. Benedict\u2019s College 2-0 in the consolation final.\n\n\u2018SpiderNail\u2019 geotechnical concept unveiled in Kandy to strengthen hill country resilience\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
